note as DEP_diagram_09_forms
  Connects to other modules via:
  specialty_chart_templates
end note

note as REC_VALUEX_FORMS_diagram_09_forms
  REC 3.4 — value[x] EXCLUSIVITY
field_values holds value_string/text/integer/decimal/boolean/date/datetime/
time/url/json/concept/reference. Add a CHECK driven by
dynamic_field_definitions.technical_data_type so only the matching value_*
column is populated per row.
end note

note as REC_POLY_FORMS_diagram_09_forms
  REC 3.1 — POLYMORPHIC REFERENCES (no DB-level FK)
field_values.(value_reference_type,value_reference_id) and
(resource_type_concept_id,resource_id) are polymorphic. Validate types
against a closed value_set and enforce via trigger; these are high-volume
so consider a concrete FK where a single target dominates.
end note

note as EXT_GOV_REF_diagram_09_forms
  EXTENSION GOVERNANCE
  Definition-set versioning, localization, provenance, access policy and
  schema migration are specified in diagram_09b_extensibility_governance.
end note

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' SOURCE CONSOLIDATED: diagram_09b_extensibility_governance.puml
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_09b_extensibility_governance
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Deep governance for dynamic fields: reusable definition sets, immutable
  schema versions, localization, provenance, access policy and safe migration.
  This extends core entities without changing their base tables or weakening
  semantic validation.
end note

